As a logistics employee, you help keep the logistics process running smoothly. You handle goods with care and make sure everything is ready for shipment. Your main tasks include:

- Handling goods: Loading, unloading, moving, and preparing products for delivery.
- Keeping order: Scanning materials, checking inventory, and organizing the workplace.
- Following rules: Working safely, following instructions, and using protective gear when needed.

- Approximately 3+ years of work-experience in a logistic environment;
- Able to communicate in English B1/B2 level;
- Driving license (car) is preferred;
- Available for working 2 shifts;
- Soft-skills that match with the company-culture: teamplayer, proactive and motivated

Mandarin Oriental Conservatorium, Amsterdam is looking for a Sous Chef to join The Lounge & Meeting and Events Kitchen. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional. Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world's most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences.As Sous Chef, you will be responsible for the following duties:
• Responsible for the internal organisation of the kitchen, including the planning of menus, overseeing all aspects of food preparation, hygiene and cost control;
• You will supervise The Lounge & Meeting and Events kitchen team;
• Delivering highest levels of quality and precision, preparing dishes in line with recipes and standards;
• Maintaining highest levels of hygiene and cost control.As Sous Chef we expect from you: 
• Passionate and quality-driven approach to cooking;
• At least two years of experience in a leadership role as Senior Chef de Partie or Junior Sous Chef;
• Teamwork, being able to work closely with 6-8 chefs on shift;
• Good knowledge of Dutch and English language (written and spoken);
• Familiar with hygiene code and HACCP regulations;
• Ability to work evenings and weekend shifts.Our commitment to you:
• A salary in scale VI of the Dutch Horeca CAO;
